{
  "id": "20261101-220021-2039",
  "hypothesis": "On this card, flash attention at head_dim 256 (tile kernel for prompt batches, vec kernel for decode, no tensor cores) is not a guaranteed win for Qwen3.5-4B the way it was at head_dim 128 on Llama. Only 8 of the 32 layers attend, so attention is a small share of decode bytes. Predictions with FA off (flash_attn 0): (a) tg128 within about \u00b12% of baseline, because decode is dominated by the ~2.7 GB weight read and the 24 DeltaNet layers, not by 8 attention layers at short context; (b) pp512 and pp2048 change measurably in one direction, which tells us whether the D=256 tile kernel is a prefill bottleneck. If pp rises with FA off, the tile kernel is under-occupied at D=256 on 10 SMs (48 KiB shared-memory limit per block); if pp drops, FA's fused softmax still pays off at D=256; (c) VRAM peak rises, because the non-FA path materialises KQ (16 heads x n_kv x ubatch 256 f32, reused across layers): roughly +20 to +100 MiB; (d) KLD and PPL stay within noise of baseline (0.024235 / 10.2405).",
  "research_objective": "Answer open question 3 from the workload brief: measure whether flash attention helps or hurts on Pascal at head_dim 256 for this hybrid model, separately for prompt (tile kernel) and decode (vec kernel). This sets the attention-path baseline before any kernel work.",
  "description": "Single-variable runtime change: runtime.flash_attn 1 -> 0. Everything else is unchanged from qwen35-4b-initial (CUDA, b12021, full offload, f16 KV, batch 2048, ubatch 256, no mmap). FA was carried over from Llama as a prior, and the brief says explicitly that the head_dim 128 result does not transfer to head_dim 256. With FA off, the 8 full-attention layers run KQ and KQV as ordinary f16-KV matmuls. On SM 6.1 llama.cpp avoids the slow FP16 path and converts to f32 for cuBLAS SGEMM, plus a separate soft_max op. Interpretation plan: the per-metric ratios for pp512 and pp2048 isolate the cost of the tile kernel. The pp2048/pp512 gap in each arm shows how much of the long-prompt slowdown comes from attention over a longer KV, which was a hypothesis in the Llama ubatch notes. tg128 shows whether the vec kernel at D=256 matters for decode at all. The VRAM delta gives the size of the materialised KQ buffer. If FA off wins on prefill but loses on decode, the follow-up is a targeted patch to the D=256 tile kernel configuration rather than a global toggle.",
